[175 AD | 484045 den | you:5175 hr | sch 24 art 75 | rep 98] > Crucible steel  [crucible_steel]
================================
tier 2, metallurgy, confidence B

Huntsman fired his crucibles with coke, which is possible only because the
steel is sealed inside a lidded clay pot: the fuel and the metal never meet,
so the sulfur cannot get in. The closed crucible is doing as much work as
the temperature. Melt blister steel in a closed crucible so the composition
homogenises and the slag separates. The crucible surviving 1600 C is the
hard part and is why this waits on good refractories. Gate on every cutting
tool, every lead screw, and therefore on all precision. CALENDAR FLOOR is
set by diffusion, not by construction: the economy needs roughly a
generation to train the trades, form the capital and build the suppliers.
Money cannot buy this down.

